{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013gqwjNSYWL3NJh8bMKVomk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t \"number\": 77,\n3\t \"title\": \"Use WS_EX_NOREDIRECTIONBITMAP to reduce memory usage when creating Windows in Microsoft Windows\",\n4\t \"body\": \"### Preflight Checklist\\n\\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) for this project.\\n- [x] I agree to follow the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) that this project adheres to.\\n- [x] I have searched the [issue tracker](https://www.github.com/electron/electron/issues) for a feature request that matches the one I want to file, without success.\\n\\n### Problem Description\\n\\nThe Windows windowing system was built with GDI, so it creates a default GDI canvas for every window. This canvas uses 3 bytes per pixel, about 6 MB for a 1080p screen. For self-rendering apps like Electron, this canvas is unnecessary. Since the memory is not allocated by the application itself but by the DWM, there is no simple way to accurately measure and test it. The only way to disable it is to pass WS_EX_NOREDIRECTIONBITMAP to CreateWindowEx. Electron Apps should use this optimization.\\n\\nBackground:\\n`microsoft/terminal#20655`\\n`microsoft/microsoft-ui-xaml#11523`\\n\\n### Proposed Solution\\n\\nUpdate the document native-code-and-electron-cpp-win32.md\\n\\n### Alternatives Considered\\n\\nnone\\n\\n### Additional Information\\n\\n_No response_\",\n5\t \"labels\": [\n6\t  \"enhancement :sparkles:\"\n7\t ],\n8\t \"state\": \"open\",\n9\t \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n10\t \"as_of\": \"2026-09-08T18:23:06Z\",\n11\t \"replay\": true\n12\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e4ce5be0-3de1-4187-bcd1-318818c0af55","uuid":"670a6f18-5e68-49ce-93f9-d74d29ab48ac","timestamp":"2026-10-23T10:03:28.733Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/runner/wor